echo
Usage: echo [-neE] [ARG]...

Print ARGs to stdout separated by spaces, followed by a newline.

	-n	no trailing newline
	-e	interpret backslash escapes (\n \t \\ \0NNN)
	-E	do not interpret escapes (default)

For anything with escapes or leading dashes, prefer printf -- echo's
handling of those varies between shells and is not portable.
